(C) Meta Tournament Analysis over n-level profiles
  profiles={4: (325, 0, 325, 325, 325), 5: (205, 0, 205, 205, 205), 6: (56, 0, 56, 56, 56)}
  n-order=[4, 5, 6]
  fingerprint={'scores': [2, 1, 0], 'score_hist': {0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1}, 'directed_cycles': 0, 'transitive_triples': 1, 'scc_sizes': [1, 1, 1], 'hamiltonian_paths': 1}

SYNTHESIS
  1. A section proof can be exact after replacing 'runner i' by the
     runner-section witness graph.  The compactified dream case is Hall
     matching; strict-open matching exposes the wall debt.
  2. The exotic cases are not mysterious: their compressed certificate is
     an open Hall packet (runner subset, section union), wall-debt sections,
     and a switch tournament on the contested sections.
  3. The tournament analogy improves when vertices are sections: section
     dominance records which regions have private support, abundant open
     witness measure, or only wall witnesses.
  4. The proof route suggested by this data is local: show every Hall packet
     has a boundary-crossing switch that strictly enlarges its section union,
     or descends to an already-proved observer-source/endpoint-mouth case.
